Z||000000||Standard||03-19-2001||03:36 PM||||The rear tires on my GT are gonna have to be replaced soon, right now they're 225/60 BFG Comp T/A's, I'm thinking about going to the stock 215/60 size.  Looking at either Sumitomo Srixon4's or another set of BFG Comp T/A's.  Both are H-rated, and I'm kinda leaning towards the Sumitomo's.  Anybody have any experience with them?<P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Everybody wants a normal life and a cool car.. <B>Most people settle for the car</B><P>I'm not dumb.  I just have a command of thoroughly useless information<BR>        <BR>AOL: LastMinuteBastrd<BR>AIM: SavedByJebus    -- you'll understand if you watch The Simpsons :D||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||03-19-2001||03:48 PM||||their ok.. but not very sticky... if your wanting a good sticky tire a Yokohama AVS Intermediate is the way to go.. the SUmitomo are ok.. i've got a friend that had them on his Mustang and they were great for tire roasting but they wouldn't ever hook up decent. I had AVSs and would pull his car casue all he'd do was smoke em.. he got a set and then i had to turn on my nitrous to smoke him..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Yokos ROCK! or a Dunlop sp8000 ||||reg||1
Z||000002||stsmithgt||03-19-2001||06:30 PM||||I have some P215/60/R15 93V M&S Michelen XGT V4 Pilots on all four corners.  I thought I compramized my traction using the V's instead of the Z's for longevity, but they've done a pretty nice job keeping me on the road also with a nice ride.||||reg||1
