Z||000009||AkursedX||04-03-2001||01:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Standard:<BR><B>That's where I'm doing my shopping right now.. the Sumitomo's are about $50 a piece.  Any opinions on the Yoko AVS db's?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I bought those last year for the rear on my 88GT  225's.  They were a pretty darn good tire (the *were* is because i got 17inch rims now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )<BR>But anyways, They have pretty good grip, but nothing great.  They have awesome wet traction, and they have real good treadlife.  Mine had about 9k miles on it and still looked fairly new.  <BR>They are a good tire if you want to sacrifice a little bit of performance for a little more life out of the tire.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Standard||04-03-2001||09:45 AM||||I think I'm gonna go with the Srixon4's.  I'll be getting them after I get paid this week.. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||fierogt88||04-03-2001||09:52 AM||||I put Sumitomo HTR100's on my 88 gt and so far I'm very happy with them.  They grip very well, I haven't heard a peep from them and I've been driving like a madman for the last couple of weeks.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>These are my first set of performance tires, though, so I really can't compare them to others.  At tirerack.com they were given similar performance numbers to Pirelli P6000's if I am remembering correctly.  There were definately tires rated better but the price/performance ratio was amazing and i had to see for myself.  So far so good.  Oh they ride comfortable to.<P>oh and they are BAD on ice.....<P>||||reg||1
